R8 is not finished, so I left it unticked in `tasks.md`. Two of the three e2e failures are fixed. The perf gate still fails most of the time on a single slow frame, which I traced but didn't fix in the time limit.

**What I fixed in `src/ui/wafer-map/WaferMapCanvas.tsx`:**
- **`wafer-stage-r6.spec.ts` (expected 2, got 4):** the probe sweep finishes during the test's zoom. At that point the verdict reveal changed state in the parent component, which re-rendered the wafer canvas. I wrapped `WaferMapCanvas` in `React.memo`, since its props from the parent don't change, so the reveal no longer re-renders the stage.
- **Visual-acceptance gap (8 px, needs ≥ 12):** the mobile mode control now sits 8 px from the top instead of 12 px, which leaves a gap of at least 12 px above the wafer disc. The other visual items (a)–(h) were already passing their checks. I marked all of them fixed in `logs/visual-acceptance.md`.

**Why the first reruns looked unchanged:** Playwright serves the existing production build from `.next` and rebuilds only if that build is missing. Until you run `pnpm build`, `pnpm e2e` tests old code. I've noted this in `logs/progress.md`.

**Results after a fresh build:**
- `pnpm typecheck`: 0 errors. `pnpm lint`: 0 errors. `pnpm test`: 34/34 files pass.
- Full `pnpm e2e` passed 13/13 once. In that run the perf gate showed 0 frames over 50 ms, median frame 16.7 ms, p95 16.8 ms, verdict visible after 936 ms, and the sweep took 1,164 ms.

**What remains:**
- **The perf gate is flaky.** In 3 of 4 isolated reruns it recorded one frame of 58–62 ms. One rerun also ran at the same time as the unit tests and got 8 slow frames, so I didn't count it.
- **The cause:** browser timing data points to the keydown handler that swaps wafers when you press ArrowRight in the wafer strip. It spends 31 ms in script and 8 ms forcing a layout, giving a frame of about 70 ms.
- **Next step:** make that swap skip the React render and avoid reading layout inside the key handler, then rerun the perf gate a few times and tick R8. This is written in `logs/progress.md`.

The R7 settle test also missed its 780 ms limit by 10 ms once (789.8 ms), then passed in the later runs. I didn't change that test.

I deleted the temporary measurement spec I used. `logs/redesign-R8-kiro.log` and `tools/kiro_cli_step.sh` were already modified before I started, and I didn't touch them.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=175

